    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "101 patients from the Endocrine Clinic, B.Y.L. Nair Hospital, Bombay, received Anovlar for 318 cycles. Follow-up was possible in only 90 for 304 cycles. In the 26 given the drug for contraception no pregnancies followed. The others were treated for various gynecological disorders. Spinbarkeit and fern tests, vaginal cytology, endometrial biopsy, basal body temperature, and urinary 17-ketosteroids were studied. Skull and chest x-rays were done when required. The drug was given orally, 1-3 tablets daily, from Day 5 to Day 25 of the normal or induced cycle. No untoward effects were noted from the higher dosage. Side effects were slight. Nausea was the most common and was relieved by antihistamines. Dysfunctional bleeding was especially benefitted by Anovlar. The drug had no ill effect on subsequent pregnancies."
    }
